//
// Each half classifies cleanly on its own; joined, every score collapses into
// the 0.62-0.69 band. interlibrary_loan has 207 exemplars against loan_policy's
// 54 and renewal's 47, and its pool legitimately talks about loan periods and
// renewing OhioLINK items, so in a flat region it edges ahead by accident.
//
// This mattered for a real reader: the wrong label pulled in the
// research-question banner (interlibrary_loan is in that set on the operator's
// 2026-07-29 rule) on a straightforward circulation answer. The banner symptom
// is separately exempted, but a wrong intent will keep costing us elsewhere.
//
// Labelled per INTENT_GUIDE: loan_policy is "loan periods, due dates in
// general, borrowing policy"; renewal is "renew checkout, extend due date". A
// question whose primary ask is how long you may keep something is loan_policy
// even when it also asks about renewing; renewal-first phrasings stay renewal.
//
// Kept to 14 entries, in line with the other dated fix files, so this does not
// simply invert the imbalance it corrects.
